## Custom Theme Builder

Users can create custom themes using RGB sliders:

### Sections

1. **Background** - Terminal background, drawer background, status bar
   - RGB range: 0-255
   - Recommended for dark themes: R=10-40, G=10-40, B=10-40

2. **Text** - Terminal text color, extra keys labels, all text
   - RGB range: 0-255
   - Recommended for contrast: R=200-255, G=200-255, B=200-255

3. **Primary** - Accent color - buttons, links, active indicators
   - RGB range: 0-255

### Workflow

1. User selects "Custom" theme from theme selector
2. "Customize Colors" button appears
3. Color picker dialog opens with three RGB slider sections
4. Preview blocks update in real-time
5. User taps "Apply" to save and reload all screens
6. Custom colors persist across app restarts (stored in preferences)

## Theme Application

- Themes apply immediately upon selection (activity recreates)
- "Follow system theme" option: Day theme when system is light, night theme when system is dark
- When "follow system" is enabled, separate day/night terminal themes can be configured
- Default theme: `dracula_plus` (applied on first use)

## Theme Persistence

- Theme selection persists across app restarts
- Custom theme RGB values stored in SharedPreferences
- Default themes are bundled and cannot be deleted
- Custom themes are marked as user-created and backed up with config export

## Impacted Components

- `android/app/src/main/java/terminal/emulator/settings/ScreenTheme.kt` - Theme selection UI
- `android/app/src/main/java/terminal/emulator/settings/ThemePreview.kt` - Theme preview component
- `native/src/terminal/ghostty_terminal/` - Any theme-related state updates
- `openspec/specs/` - This specification entry

## Non-Goals

- Full CSS-style theming engine
- Per-cell color customization
- Dynamic theme animation transitions (beyond simple switch)